<title>NETHERLANDS: PHILIPS U.S. VACUUM CLEANER ACTIVITIES END.</title>
<headline>PHILIPS U.S. VACUUM CLEANER ACTIVITIES END.</headline>
<dateline>EINDHOVEN, Netherlands 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Electronics NV said on Friday it would stop its vacuum cleaner activities in the United States.</p>
<p>It said that as a result of this move, 300 jobs would be lost at the Regina plant in Long Beach, Mississippi, where vacuum cleaner production would stop at the end of the year.</p>
<p>Philips will retain ownership of the Regina brand name and may re-establish a position in U.S. floor care in the future.</p>
<p>&quot;Philips will focus on continuing to grow its floor care position in Europe,&quot; it added.</p>
